 "cover": "Five waves of outside power, read through Van Vollenhoven, and the island where they arrived late, thin, or as extraction.",
 "intro": "Draft for the Research Conversation (24 Nov 2026), after Eva's request of 20 November: show the geography of Indonesia, then how its history unfolded, so that the choice of Sumba makes sense. The spine is Van Vollenhoven's own argument that adat grew from an Austronesian base onto which Hindu-Buddhist, Islamic, Chinese and Western elements were laid. Each slide asks the same two questions: where did this wave land hardest, and what reached Sumba?",
