   "id": "s02",
   "label": "c. 2000 BCE – 500 CE",
   "title": "The base layer",
   "text": "Van Vollenhoven begins his account of adat with a time before any foreign influence, when only the indigenous law of the Malayo-Polynesians existed in the archipelago. Bellwood traces those Austronesian speakers south from Taiwan through the Philippines and Sulawesi into the island chains. Sumba shares this base with the rest of the archipelago. What differs from island to island is how much was laid on top.",
