   "text": "Van Vollenhoven dates the Hindu contribution to adat from the eighth century, after Hindu civilisation reached Java. Coedès places the earliest Indonesian inscriptions at Kutai in Borneo. Wolters argues that local rulers chose and localised Indian ideas rather than receiving them whole. The map shows where that layer settled: along the western sea lanes, in Sumatra, Java and Bali. Nothing marks it on Sumba.",
