   "id": "s04",
   "label": "1365",
   "title": "A name on Majapahit's list",
   "text": "The Deśawarṇana, a court poem of 1365 translated by Robson, lists Sumba among the lands that paid homage to Majapahit. It is a court record, and Ricklefs warns that such lists show the reach of a court's imagination more than its rule. For Sumba, this is the first appearance in a written source, and it comes as a name on someone else's list.\n\nMore: Check before presenting: the exact canto and verse where Sumba appears in Robson's translation (it is usually given as canto 14). This slide is the first instance of a pattern the rest of the story repeats: Sumba is claimed from outside long before it is governed.",
