   "id": "s09",
   "label": "1901 – 1919",
   "title": "Codifying adat while conquering Sumba",
   "text": "Holleman shows Van Vollenhoven fighting a 1904 bill to unify all law on the Dutch Civil Code, then, in 1919, a bill for Western-style land ownership that suited plantations. Burns shows how his school mapped the Indies into adat law circles. In the same years troops pacified Sumba, governed from Kupang as part of the Residency of Timor. Adat was being written down for the colony while Sumba was conquered.\n\nMore: Next step for the drawing: Van Vollenhoven's nineteen adat law circles, with Sumba inside the Timor group. Take the list and map from Holleman's edition before drawing it; the app does not yet hold that boundary.",
