   "title": "Why Sumba",
   "text": "Read through Van Vollenhoven's layers, Sumba is unusual. The Hindu-Buddhist and Chinese waves barely touched it, Islam stayed on its coast, and the West came first as a slave trade and late as a government. Keane and Vel describe an island where ancestral ritual and clan still order land and status. That makes Sumba a place to see how indigenous space is made and defended when each new power claims it.\n\nMore: This is the argument of the thesis, not a finding of the sources. It leads straight into the research questions slide.",
